      "writtenOn": "2022-06-30T19:17:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry it took me a long time to come back to this. I think there\u0027s a bug in this patch when CONFIG_RT_SOFTINT_OPTIMIZATION is not set.\n\nSpecifically this hunk\n\n```\n  -\n  -               wakeup_softirqd();\n          }\n \n  +#ifdef CONFIG_RT_SOFTINT_OPTIMIZATION\n  +       if (pending | deferred)\n  +               wakeup_softirqd(); \n  +#endif\n```\n\nwhere wakeup_softirqd() will never be called if CONFIG_RT_SOFTINT_OPTIMIZATION is not set. Is the ifdef guard actually required here? It must be removed AFAICT to preserve the behavior of the code when this is not set.\n\nI believe LONG_SOFTIRQ_MASK should be defined to 0 when this config option is not set OR compile out softirq_deferred_for_rt() function so that it never clear pending or set deferred.",
      "parentUuid": "557e625e_5eae165c",
      "revId": "0578248bedae9a6b7bd4325f06101332c29af962",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
